# Citation metadata for ARPAHLS/aura.
# Validate: pip install cffconvert && cffconvert -i CITATION.cff -f apalike
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
  Record the machine-aura version you used (PyPI or Git tag) for reproducibility.
type: software
title: AURA
abstract: >-
  AURA (machine-aura) is an open-source Python verifiable runtime coat and
  attestation spine for AI agents. It wraps existing hosts with a membrane
  model — ingress context, egress policy on tool calls, prescriptive sequencer
  pipelines, observers, hash-chained audit trails, conformance summaries, and
  offline-verifiable signed audit packs — without replacing the user's loop,
  model, or skill runtime.
version: "0.3.7"
date-released: "2026-11-21"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ARPAHLS/aura"
url: "https://github.com/ARPAHLS/aura"
